<title>USA: Fed adds temporary reserves via 4-day system RP.</title>
<headline>Fed adds temporary reserves via 4-day system RP.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Thursday through four-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had anticipated a multi-day system repurchase operation.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-1/2 percent, the Fed's target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>-- (( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
